# rejects.csv is a run byproduct of normalize_vendor_seed.py - it holds
# the RAW, UNREDACTED vendor-sheet rows the normalizer rejected, verbatim,
# including exactly the phone/email-shaped text that got them rejected in
# the first place (see looks_like_pii() / _PII_CHECKED_FIELDS in
# backend/core/scripts/normalize_vendor_seed.py).
#
# This directory's whole design point is PII-free BY CONSTRUCTION - not
# by discipline ("remember not to commit it"). Once someone runs the
# tool against the owner's real vendor sheet before D27, a plain
# `git add -A` must not be able to smuggle real phone numbers/emails into
# git history. Do not remove this entry: regenerate rejects.csv locally,
# inspect it, then delete it - never commit it.
rejects.csv
